course: dictionary
lesson: 6254
title: Molars: the grinding teeth
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your teeth have different jobs. The front teeth cut, the pointed teeth tear, and the wide teeth at the back grind. Those wide back teeth are called molars. «Molars at the back grind and crush food.» Grind means to crush food into small bits so you can swallow it.
explain: Molar can be a noun or an adjective. A molar is one tooth, and molar can also describe a tooth: a molar tooth is a back tooth. Use the clues around the word. The sentence says the molars are at the back, and they grind and crush, so you know what kind of tooth they are.
explain: Sentences about teeth can use phrases you may not know, like «six-year molars». Read on for the clues: they come in at about age six, behind the baby teeth. Even if you did not know the word six-year, the words around it tell you it is a kind of molar. When in doubt, check a dictionary or ask your science teacher.
fact: A molar is a large, flat-topped tooth at the back of your mouth.
fact: Molars grind and crush food so that it can be swallowed.
fact: «The six-year molars come in behind the baby teeth without any baby tooth falling out.»
fact: A grown-up set has 12 molars, and wisdom teeth are the last of these, also called third molars.
fact: Food can get stuck in the grooves of molars, so dentists may put sealants on them.
fact: Elephants get six sets of big molars, one after another, during their lives.
exercise: «Molars at the back grind and crush food.» What do molars do? | Cut food at the front | Smell food from far away | *Grind and crush food | Tear meat into strips
exercise: Which teeth come in at about age six, behind the baby teeth? | Canines | Baby molars | Wisdom teeth | *The six-year molars
exercise: «There are different teeth for different jobs: sharp incisors at the front cut, pointed canines tear, and wide molars at the back grind.» Find and copy the word for the teeth that grind. | incisors | *molars | canines | jobs
test: A grown-up set has 8 incisors, 4 canines, 8 premolars and how many molars? | 4 | *12 | 8 | 32
test: Which animal gets six sets of big molars, one after another? | Crocodile | Shark | *Elephant | Human
exam: «Food can get stuck in the grooves of molars, so dentists may put sealants on them.» Why might dentists put sealants on molars? | Molars are used for cutting | *Food gets stuck in their grooves, so they can get cavities | Sealants make teeth grow longer | Molars are too small to see
